Sval: Space after an @ word picks the engine Tab would

Tab completes an @ word to the first engine with a keyword the word
begins (UrlbarProviderTokenAliasEngines), while Space searched only an
engine whose whole keyword the word is (UrlbarProviderAliasEngines), so
"@k" and Space searched the default engine for "@k" where Tab picked
Kagi. Both keys take their engine from SvalSearchKeywords, which also
lets a whole keyword win over a longer one it begins, so "@b" picks
Bing ahead of Brave Search's "@br".

